---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StopShield from '../components/illus/StopShield.astro';
import RScale from '../components/illus/RScale.astro';
import Horizon from '../components/illus/Horizon.astro';
import Distribution from '../components/illus/Distribution.astro';
import LayoutMosaic from '../components/illus/LayoutMosaic.astro';
import RCalendar from '../components/illus/RCalendar.astro';
---
<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <img src="/wortmarke.svg" alt="FixedR" width="243" height="90" />
    <p class="tagline">your trading cockpit.</p>
    <h1>The trading cockpit that shows you risk, not&nbsp;money.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Built for prop traders. Every position starts from a fixed stop-loss, every result is
      measured in <span class="r-value">R</span> — and the one number that makes you tilt
      never appears on screen.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a class="btn" href="/waitlist">Join the waitlist</a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="/manifesto">Why no money?</a>
    </p>
    <p style="color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem;">Windows app · works with MetaTrader &amp; NinjaTrader</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 style="text-align:center">Six mechanics. One purpose: keep you inside your rules.</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <StopShield />
        <h3>Mandatory stop-loss</h3>
        <p>No stop, no trade. The risk of every position is fixed before entry — not negotiated with yourself afterwards.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <RScale />
        <h3>Position size from risk</h3>
        <p>You decide the fraction of the account to risk. FixedR computes the lot size from your stop distance. Backwards — the only sane direction.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <Horizon />
        <h3>Money stays out of sight</h3>
        <p>Results, targets, drawdown — everything is denominated in R. What you don't stare at can't make you tilt.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <Distribution />
        <h3>One trade, many accounts</h3>
        <p>Place a trade once, distribute it across your funded accounts by rule. If an account isn't configured, FixedR refuses loudly — it never guesses.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <LayoutMosaic />
        <h3>Multi-monitor layouts</h3>
        <p>Charts, journal, risk panel — arranged across screens the way a cockpit arranges instruments: everything where your eyes expect it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <RCalendar />
        <h3>The R calendar</h3>
        <p>Your month in R, day by day. Progress you can compare across accounts, account sizes and years.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="callout">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0.4rem">Why no money?</h2>
    <p>
      Prop trading is a percentage game: drawdown limits, profit targets, consistency rules —
      all defined relative to account size. The money number adds nothing but emotion.
      FixedR removes it entirely. Not a setting. Not a toggle. It's simply not there.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/manifesto">Read the manifesto →</a></p>
  </section>

  <section style="text-align:center; padding: 2rem 0 3rem;">
    <h2>Built local-first</h2>
    <p style="max-width: 34rem; margin: 0.8rem auto;">
      FixedR runs on your machine. Your journal and account data live in a local database —
      this website doesn't track you either.
    </p>
    <p><a class="btn" href="/waitlist">Join the waitlist</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
